SUMMARY:Step Inside Historic Central Fire Station
DESCRIPTION:Central Fire Station: A Centennial Reflection\nA photographic exhibition exploring the lives\, work\, and traditions of Greensboro firefighters\, 1926–1980. \nStep inside the historic station where generations of Greensboro firefighters lived\, worked\, and served their community. Through photographs taken in and around the building and firsthand recollections from firefighters\, discover the daily routines\, relationships\, skills\, and traditions that shaped life at Central Fire Station. \nUPCOMING PUBLIC OPEN HOURS\nFriday\, November 6 | 5–8 PM\nDuring Downtown Greensboro’s First Friday \nFriday\, December 4 | 5–9 PM\nDuring Downtown Greensboro’s Festival of Lights \nFREE ADMISSION \nHistoric Central Fire Station | Downtown Greensboro \nEntrance on N. Greene Street\, through the Greensboro Marriott Downtown. \nPresented in celebration of the Greensboro Fire Department’s Centennial\, 1926–2026. \nAn exhibition developed through the collaboration of the Greensboro Fire Department\, Greensboro Firefighter Historical Society\, North Carolina Folklife Institute\, and Marriott Greensboro Downtown. \nSupported in part by North Carolina Humanities\, the state affiliate of the National Endowment for the Humanities.
URL:https://nchumanities.org/event/step-inside-historic-central-fire-station/
LOCATION:Central Fire Station\, 318 N. Greene St.\, Greensboro\, NC\, 27401\, United States
CATEGORIES:NC Humanities Grantee Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nchumanities.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Central-Fire-Station-Exhibit-Flyer-1.png
ORGANIZER;CN="North Carolina Folklife Institute":MAILTO:staff@ncfolk.org
END:VEVENT
